{"assumptions":["ASM-19: The API endpoints are GET /api/parts (q, category, brand, page), GET /api/parts/brands, POST /api/orders, GET /api/orders (status), GET /api/orders/{orderNumber} and POST /api/orders/{orderNumber}/cancel. Paths can be renamed as long as the behaviour stays the same.","ASM-20: Cart and checkout logic in the React app sits in public client classes CartStore (addPart, setQuantity, removeLine, lines, count, subtotal, totals, applyStockLimits, refresh) and CheckoutForm (canPlaceOrder, startSubmit, finishSubmit), so it can be unit-tested directly; CartStore.refresh takes a parts API client so the outbound call can be stubbed.","ASM-21: API error statuses are 400 for invalid input, 404 for an order that doesn't exist or belongs to another buyer, and 409 for stock or cancel conflicts. Session handling is left to the existing company login (Q-4).","ASM-22: A quantity that isn't a whole number is rounded to the nearest whole number before being limited to 1–99 (from ASM-12).","ASM-23: Pressing \"Add to cart\" when the line quantity already equals the part's stock leaves the quantity unchanged and shows \"Only n available\", the same as REQ-14.","ASM-24: The order total is calculated on the server from current part prices and the delivery charge. Prices and totals the client sends are ignored.","ASM-25: When a cart line's part is found to have 0 stock (on a 409 stock conflict or when the cart opens), the line is removed from the cart rather than set to quantity 0, with the message \"<part name> is now out of stock\", so every remaining line keeps a quantity of 1–99 (settled by Q-1).","ASM-26: When the cart opens, CartStore.refresh reads the current price and stock of the cart's parts from the existing parts API (GET /api/parts filtered to the cart's part numbers); any price saved in local storage is never shown (Q-3).","ASM-27: The network-error message text is \"Your order may have been placed. Check My orders before trying again.\"; the exact wording can change as long as it tells the buyer to check My orders before retrying (Q-2).","ASM-28: When the parts API call in CartStore.refresh fails (network error or 5xx status), refresh returns a result with an error field set, lines() returns each line's name, part number and quantity with unitPrice and lineTotal null, and subtotal() and totals() return null until a later refresh succeeds; the cart lines and quantities are kept unchanged (Q-5). The exact error message wording is free."],"critic":[{"finding":"ASM-26 and AC-41.1 need GET /api/parts filtered to the cart's part numbers in a single call, but REQ-2/4/5 and ASM-19 only define q (at least 2 characters, substring match), category, brand and page, so no defined parameter can fetch exactly the cart's parts.","reqId":"REQ-41","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"When the cart opens, only lines whose part now has 0 stock are handled; a line whose stock has dropped but is still above 0 (cart quantity 5, stock now 2) is left unclamped until the 409 at Place order, and REQ-14's clamp only runs when the buyer edits the quantity.","reqId":"REQ-42","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Nothing covers a cart line whose part number is missing from the parts API response (part deleted or renamed); refresh behaviour, the price shown and checkout availability are all undefined for that line.","reqId":"REQ-42","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The order is charged at the server's current price, but the price can change between cart refresh and Place order; nothing says the buyer is told or asked to confirm, so the saved total can differ from the total on screen (payments risk).","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"There is no error or loading path for Find parts or My orders when GET /api/parts or GET /api/orders fails; only the cart's price fetch (REQ-43) and place-order (REQ-24) have failure behaviour.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"There is no UI behaviour for a cancel request that fails with a network or 5xx error; only the 409 path (REQ-34) is specified.","reqId":"REQ-32","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The timeline is defined only as Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered, so what a Cancelled order (reachable through REQ-33) shows is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-31","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The status filter has no behaviour for an unknown status value (for example ?status=Foo) and no UI acceptance criterion for the filter control on My orders.","reqId":"REQ-29","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The requirement lists unknown part number as a 400 case, but no acceptance criterion exercises it.","reqId":"REQ-21","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"NFR-1 widens the 2-second target from I-8 (the parts page with 5,000 parts) to all three screens at 1,000 concurrent users, yet ASM-16 only says up to 1,000 users in total, and REQ-38 measures /parts with a single tester.","reqId":"NFR-1","rubric":4,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The 409 handling is checked only through CartStore unit criteria; no criterion shows the portal displaying \"Only n available\" or \"<part name> is now out of stock\" to the buyer, or keeping the address and delivery option after a 409.","reqId":"REQ-39","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-10.2 expects the buyer to tab to a disabled \"Add to cart\" button, but natively disabled buttons cannot receive focus, so the check cannot be carried out as written.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":1,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"95th-percentile time from navigation start until content is shown is under 2,000 ms for /parts, /cart and /orders, measured at 1,000 concurrent users","text":"Each of the three screens loads with 5,000 parts in the parts database."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"Supports 1,000 buyers and 100,000 order and order-line records with NFR-1 still met","text":"Capacity for the first year."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 serious or critical violations in an automated axe scan of each screen, plus 100% of fields with labels and 100% of stock and status indicators carrying text","text":"WCAG 2.1 AA compliance on all three screens; colour is never the only signal for stock state or order status."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"0 horizontal scroll at viewport widths of 360, 768 and 1280 px","text":"Responsive layout."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"100% of ui and manual acceptance criteria pass on the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox","text":"Browser support."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"100% of prices shown as £ with exactly 2 decimals; 0 non-English text strings","text":"English only; prices in GBP."}],"outOfScope":["Sign-in and accounts (the existing company login is used as-is)","A separate requirement that the API rejects requests without a valid company-login session with status 401; the existing company login is relied on as-is (Q-4)","Payments and invoices","Admin or staff screens, including changing an order's status after Placed (ASM-6)","Adding or editing parts","Stock management, including changing stock when orders are placed or cancelled (ASM-2)","Returns","Emails and notifications","Multiple or saved delivery addresses (ASM-15)","Discounts","Vehicle (VIN) lookup","Reports","Mobile apps","Other languages or currencies","Integrations with other systems"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in buyer","id":"AC-1.1","level":"manual","then":"Each URL shows its screen (Find parts, Cart and checkout, My orders), and the header on each screen has links to the other two","when":"they open /parts, /cart and /orders in turn"},{"given":"A signed-in buyer on /orders","id":"AC-1.2","level":"manual","then":"The order detail panel is shown on the same /orders page and no other page opens","when":"they open an order"}],"ears":"The portal shall provide exactly three screens for the signed-in buyer: Find parts at /parts, Cart and checkout at /cart, and My orders at /orders with the order detail panel on the same page.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"45 parts in the parts database","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned list has 20 parts in name A–Z order, each with fields image, name, partNumber, brand, price, stockState and stock, and the response total count is 45","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?page=1"},{"given":"45 parts in the parts database","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list has 5 parts, the last 5 by name A–Z","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?page=3"},{"given":"A part with price 12.5 and no image","id":"AC-2.3","level":"api","then":"That part's price value is returned as 12.50 and its image field is null","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts"},{"given":"Part BP-200 with stock quantity 4 in the parts database","id":"AC-2.4","level":"api","then":"The returned BP-200 record has stock value 4 and stockState value \"Low stock (4 left)\"","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts"}],"ears":"When a buyer requests the parts list, the parts API shall return parts sorted by name A–Z, 20 per page, each with image (or none), name, part number, brand, price in GBP with 2 decimals, stock state and stock quantity as a whole number.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-9","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Parts with stock 5, 4, 1 and 0","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The returned stockState values are \"In stock\", \"Low stock (4 left)\", \"Low stock (1 left)\" and \"Out of stock\"","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts"},{"given":"A part with stock 120","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The returned stockState value is \"In stock\"","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts"}],"ears":"The parts API shall set a part's stock state to \"In stock\" when stock is 5 or more, \"Low stock (n left)\" when stock is 1 to 4, and \"Out of stock\" when stock is 0.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-7","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Parts named \"Oil Filter\" (part number OF-100) and \"Brake Pad\" (part number BP-200)","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only \"Oil Filter\"","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?q=oil"},{"given":"The same parts","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only \"Brake Pad\"","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?q=bp-2"},{"given":"The same parts","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains both parts, so no search filter is applied","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?q=o (1 character)"}],"ears":"When the search text has at least 2 characters, the parts API shall return only parts whose name or part number contains that text, ignoring letter case.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Parts: Bosch Brakes \"Brake Pad\", Bosch Filters \"Oil Filter\", Mann Filters \"Air Filter\"","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only \"Oil Filter\"","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?category=Filters&brand=Bosch"},{"given":"The same parts","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains only \"Air Filter\"","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?category=Filters&q=air"},{"given":"The same parts","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The returned list contains all 3 parts","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?category=All&brand=All"},{"given":"The same parts","id":"AC-5.4","level":"api","then":"The returned list is [\"Bosch\", \"Mann\"], taken from the parts data","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts/brands"}],"ears":"When the buyer picks a category or brand filter, the parts API shall return only parts matching that one category and that one brand, combined with any search text, where \"All\" means no filter.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The buyer is on page 3 of Find parts","id":"AC-6.1","level":"manual","then":"Page 1 of the filtered results is shown","when":"they change the category filter"}],"ears":"When the search text or a filter changes on Find parts, the portal shall show page 1 of the results.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No part contains the text \"zzzz\"","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty with total count 0","when":"the buyer calls GET /api/parts?q=zzzz"},{"given":"The buyer has searched \"zzzz\" with category Brakes on Find parts","id":"AC-7.2","level":"manual","then":"\"No parts match\" is shown with a clear button, and pressing it empties the search box, sets both filters to All and shows page 1 of all parts","when":"the results load"}],"ears":"When no part matches the search and filters, the portal shall show \"No parts match\" and a button that clears the search and filters.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An empty CartStore and a part with stock 10","id":"AC-8.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned lines list has one line for that part with quantity value 1","when":"CartStore.addPart(part) is called"},{"given":"A CartStore holding that part with quantity 2","id":"AC-8.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned lines list still has one line for that part, with quantity value 3","when":"CartStore.addPart(part) is called"},{"given":"A CartStore holding that part with quantity equal to its stock (10)","id":"AC-8.3","level":"unit","then":"The line quantity value stays 10 and the returned message is \"Only 10 available\"","when":"CartStore.addPart(part) is called"}],"ears":"When the buyer presses \"Add to cart\" on a part that is in stock, the cart shall add a line with quantity 1, or raise the existing line's quantity by 1.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore with 2 of a filter and 1 of a brake pad","id":"AC-9.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is 3","when":"CartStore.count() is called"},{"given":"The header shows cart count 3 on Find parts","id":"AC-9.2","level":"manual","then":"The header cart count shown changes to 4 without a page reload","when":"the buyer presses \"Add to cart\" on an in-stock part"}],"ears":"The portal shall show in the header a cart count equal to the total of all quantities in the cart, updated whenever the cart changes.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An empty CartStore and a part with stock 0","id":"AC-10.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned lines list is empty","when":"CartStore.addPart(part) is called"},{"given":"Find parts lists a part with stock 0","id":"AC-10.2","level":"manual","then":"The button is shown disabled and pressing it leaves the header cart count value unchanged","when":"the buyer views or tabs to that part's \"Add to cart\" button"}],"ears":"If a part is out of stock, then the portal shall disable its \"Add to cart\" button.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore holding 3 of part BP-200 \"Brake Pad\" at £12.50","id":"AC-11.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned line has name \"Brake Pad\", partNumber \"BP-200\", unitPrice 12.50, quantity 3 and lineTotal 37.50","when":"CartStore.lines() is called"}],"ears":"The cart shall give each line its name, part number, unit price, quantity and line total, where line total = unit price × quantity.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore holding 1 of a £12.50 part and 1 of a £5.00 part","id":"AC-12.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned lineTotal for that line is 50.00 and CartStore.subtotal() returns 55.00","when":"CartStore.setQuantity(\"BP-200\", 4) is called for the £12.50 part"},{"given":"The Cart screen with a line at quantity 1","id":"AC-12.2","level":"manual","then":"The line total and the order total shown update without pressing any other button","when":"the buyer types 4 in the quantity field"}],"ears":"When the buyer changes a line quantity, the cart shall recalculate that line total and the order totals at once.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore line for a part with stock 500","id":"AC-13.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned quantity values are 1, 1, 99 and 3","when":"CartStore.setQuantity is called with \"\", 0, 150 and 2.6 in turn"}],"ears":"If the buyer enters a quantity that is blank, 0, above 99 or not a whole number, then the cart shall set it to the nearest whole number from 1 to 99.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore line for a part with stock 4","id":"AC-14.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned quantity value is 4 and the returned message is \"Only 4 available\"","when":"CartStore.setQuantity(partNumber, 7) is called"},{"given":"The Cart screen with a line for a part with stock 4","id":"AC-14.2","level":"manual","then":"The field shows 4 and \"Only 4 available\" is displayed next to the line","when":"the buyer types 7 in the quantity field"}],"ears":"If the buyer enters a quantity above the part's stock, then the cart shall set the quantity to the stock quantity and give the message \"Only n available\".","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore with lines BP-200 and OF-100","id":"AC-15.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned lines list contains only OF-100 and CartStore.count() returns OF-100's quantity","when":"CartStore.removeLine(\"BP-200\") is called"}],"ears":"When the buyer presses \"Remove\" on a cart line, the cart shall remove that line.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore for buyer B1 holding 2 of OF-100, using a given local storage","id":"AC-16.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned list holds 2 of OF-100","when":"a new CartStore is created for buyer B1 with the same local storage and lines() is called"},{"given":"The same local storage holding buyer B1's cart","id":"AC-16.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned list is empty","when":"a new CartStore is created for buyer B2 and lines() is called"}],"ears":"The cart shall keep its lines in the browser's local storage under the signed-in buyer's ID, so the cart survives page reloads on the same device.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer with an empty cart","id":"AC-17.1","level":"manual","then":"\"Your cart is empty\" and a link to /parts are shown, and no address field, delivery option or \"Place order\" button is displayed","when":"they open /cart"}],"ears":"While the cart is empty, the portal shall show \"Your cart is empty\" with a link to Find parts and hide checkout.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","ASM-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CheckoutForm with delivery option Standard","id":"AC-18.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned values are false, true, true and false","when":"CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called with addresses of 4, 5, 200 and 201 characters in turn"},{"given":"A CheckoutForm with a 20-character address and no delivery option","id":"AC-18.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is false","when":"CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called"},{"given":"A buyer who placed an earlier order","id":"AC-18.3","level":"manual","then":"The delivery address field is shown empty","when":"they open checkout again"}],"ears":"The checkout shall enable \"Place order\" only when the delivery address has 5 to 200 characters and a delivery option (Standard or Next day) is selected.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore with subtotal 37.50","id":"AC-19.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is subtotal 37.50, deliveryCharge 9.99, total 47.49","when":"CartStore.totals(\"NEXT_DAY\") is called"},{"given":"A CartStore with subtotal 37.50","id":"AC-19.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is subtotal 37.50, deliveryCharge 0.00, total 37.50","when":"CartStore.totals(\"STANDARD\") is called"}],"ears":"The checkout shall show subtotal, delivery charge (Standard £0.00, Next day £9.99) and total, where total = subtotal + delivery charge.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-7","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B1, no earlier orders in the database, part BP-200 at £12.50 with stock 10","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the response body has orderNumber \"ORD-000001\", status \"Placed\" and total 34.99","when":"B1 calls POST /api/orders with lines [{partNumber: BP-200, quantity: 2}], address \"1 High St, Leeds\", deliveryOption NEXT_DAY"},{"given":"The order from AC-20.1","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"There is one orders row for buyer B1 with ORD-000001, date placed, address, deliveryOption NEXT_DAY, total 34.99, status Placed, and one order_lines row with partNumber BP-200, quantity 2, unitPrice 12.50","when":"the orders and order_lines tables are read"},{"given":"ORD-000001 exists","id":"AC-20.3","level":"api","then":"The returned orderNumber is \"ORD-000002\"","when":"another valid order is placed"},{"given":"A client sends unitPrice 1.00 for BP-200 priced £12.50","id":"AC-20.4","level":"api","then":"The saved order_lines row has unitPrice 12.50, so the sent price value is ignored","when":"it calls POST /api/orders"}],"ears":"When the buyer places an order with valid lines, address and delivery option, the orders API shall save an order with status Placed, a sequential order number ORD- followed by 6 zero-padded digits, each line's current part price as unit price, and total = subtotal + delivery charge.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-7","ASM-8","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B1","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the orders table row count is unchanged","when":"B1 calls POST /api/orders with an empty lines list and otherwise valid fields"},{"given":"Buyer B1","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 400 with an error field naming the invalid input, and the orders table row count is unchanged","when":"B1 calls POST /api/orders with a 4-character address, then a 201-character address, then deliveryOption \"EXPRESS\", then quantity 0"}],"ears":"If a place-order request has no lines, a quantity outside 1–99, an unknown part number, an address outside 5–200 characters, or a missing or unknown delivery option, then the orders API shall reject it with status 400 and save no order.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-5","ASM-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Part BP-200 with stock 3 and part OF-100 with stock 0","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409, the response lists {BP-200, available 3} and {OF-100, available 0}, and the orders table row count is unchanged","when":"B1 calls POST /api/orders with BP-200 quantity 5 and OF-100 quantity 1"}],"ears":"If any line's quantity is above the part's stock when an order is placed, then the orders API shall reject the order with status 409 and return each affected part number with the stock now available, saving no order.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer with 3 items in the cart and a valid address and delivery option","id":"AC-23.1","level":"manual","then":"\"ORD-000007\" is displayed, the header cart count shows 0, and reloading /cart shows \"Your cart is empty\"","when":"they press \"Place order\" and the API returns ORD-000007"}],"ears":"When an order is placed successfully, the portal shall empty the cart and show the new order number.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer at checkout with 2 lines, an address and Next day selected, and the API returning status 500","id":"AC-24.1","level":"manual","then":"An error message is shown, the 2 lines, the address and Next day are still displayed, and \"Place order\" is enabled","when":"they press \"Place order\""},{"given":"A buyer at checkout with 2 lines, an address and Standard selected, and the POST /api/orders request failing with a network error (no response)","id":"AC-24.2","level":"manual","then":"The message \"Your order may have been placed. Check My orders before trying again.\" is shown, the 2 lines, the address and Standard are still displayed, and \"Place order\" is enabled","when":"they press \"Place order\""}],"ears":"If placing an order fails with a network error or a server error, then the portal shall show an error message, which for a network error tells the buyer to check My orders before retrying, and keep the cart lines, address and delivery option so the buyer can try again.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-11","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Part BP-200 with stock 10","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"The parts row for BP-200 still has stock value 10 after each call","when":"B1 places an order for 2 of BP-200 and then cancels it through the API"}],"ears":"The orders API shall leave the stock quantity in the parts database unchanged when an order is placed or cancelled.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B1 has 2 orders and buyer B2 has 3 orders","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list has exactly B1's 2 orders","when":"B1 calls GET /api/orders"},{"given":"Order ORD-000005 belongs to B2","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 404 and the order row status is unchanged","when":"B1 calls GET /api/orders/ORD-000005 and POST /api/orders/ORD-000005/cancel"}],"ears":"The orders API shall return to a buyer only the orders placed by that buyer.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"B1 placed ORD-000001 on 1 Oct (2 filters + 1 pad) and ORD-000002 on 3 Oct","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list is ORD-000002 then ORD-000001, and ORD-000001 has fields datePlaced, itemCount 3, total and status","when":"B1 calls GET /api/orders"}],"ears":"When a buyer requests their orders, the orders API shall return them newest first, each with order number, date placed, number of items (total of all quantities), total and status.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"B1 has orders with statuses Placed, Placed and Cancelled","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"The returned list has only the 1 Cancelled order","when":"B1 calls GET /api/orders?status=Cancelled"}],"ears":"When the buyer picks a status filter on My orders, the orders API shall return only that buyer's orders with that status.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"B1's order ORD-000001 with 2 of BP-200 at £12.50, Next day, address \"1 High St, Leeds\"","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response has the line {BP-200, Brake Pad, 2, 12.50}, address \"1 High St, Leeds\", deliveryOption NEXT_DAY, total 34.99 and status Placed","when":"B1 calls GET /api/orders/ORD-000001"}],"ears":"When a buyer opens one of their orders, the orders API shall return its lines (part number, name, quantity, unit price), delivery address, delivery option, total and status.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order whose status was set to Dispatched in the database","id":"AC-31.1","level":"manual","then":"The timeline shown lists the four steps in order, and Dispatched is marked as current with a text label, not by colour alone","when":"the buyer opens it on My orders"}],"ears":"When the buyer opens an order, the portal shall show a status timeline Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered with the current status marked by text as well as colour.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-7","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order with status Placed and one with status Packed","id":"AC-32.1","level":"manual","then":"\"Cancel order\" is shown only for the Placed order","when":"the buyer opens each one"},{"given":"The buyer pressed \"Cancel order\" on a Placed order","id":"AC-32.2","level":"manual","then":"No cancel request is sent after declining; after confirming, the status shown becomes Cancelled and the button is no longer displayed","when":"they decline the confirmation, then press it again and confirm"}],"ears":"While an order's status is Placed, the portal shall show a \"Cancel order\" button in the order detail that asks for confirmation before calling the cancel API.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"B1's order ORD-000001 with status Placed","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the response status field is \"Cancelled\", and the orders row has status Cancelled","when":"B1 calls POST /api/orders/ORD-000001/cancel"}],"ears":"When a buyer cancels their order whose status is still Placed, the orders API shall set the status to Cancelled.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"B1's order ORD-000001 whose status was changed to Packed in the database","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 with an error message, and the orders row status is still Packed","when":"B1 calls POST /api/orders/ORD-000001/cancel"},{"given":"The buyer has an order open showing Placed, and its status was changed to Packed in the database","id":"AC-34.2","level":"manual","then":"A message is shown saying the order can no longer be cancelled, the panel refreshes to show Packed, and \"Cancel order\" is no longer displayed","when":"they press \"Cancel order\" and confirm"}],"ears":"If the order's status is no longer Placed when the buyer confirms cancelling, then the orders API shall refuse with status 409 and leave the status unchanged.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B3 with no orders","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty","when":"B3 calls GET /api/orders"},{"given":"Buyer B3 with no orders","id":"AC-35.2","level":"manual","then":"\"No orders yet\" and a link to /parts are shown","when":"they open /orders"}],"ears":"While the buyer has no orders, the portal shall show \"No orders yet\" and a link to Find parts on My orders.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox","id":"AC-36.1","level":"manual","then":"No horizontal scroll bar is shown and every button and field is displayed and usable","when":"each screen is opened at 360 px, 768 px and 1280 px widths"}],"ears":"The portal shall show all three screens without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360 px upwards.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The three screens with a cart containing 2 lines","id":"AC-37.1","level":"manual","then":"Every step can be completed, focus is always visible, and every field has a label announced by a screen reader","when":"a tester uses only the keyboard to search, filter, add to cart, change quantity, remove, place an order, open an order and cancel it"}],"ears":"The portal shall give every form field a visible text label and let the buyer reach and use every control by keyboard alone.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"5,000 parts seeded in the parts database","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"The 95th-percentile response time is under 500 ms and each response status is 200","when":"GET /api/parts?page=1&q=filter&category=Filters is called 100 times"},{"given":"5,000 parts seeded and a cold browser cache on a desktop with a 10 Mbps connection","id":"AC-38.2","level":"manual","then":"The first 20 parts are displayed within 2 seconds of navigation start","when":"a tester opens /parts"}],"ears":"While the parts database holds 5,000 parts, the Find parts screen shall load its first page of results in under 2 seconds.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore holding 5 of BP-200, 1 of OF-100 \"Oil Filter\" and 2 of AF-300","id":"AC-39.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned lines list has BP-200 with quantity value 3 and message \"Only 3 available\", AF-300 with quantity value 2, and no OF-100 line; the returned messages include \"Oil Filter is now out of stock\"","when":"CartStore.applyStockLimits([{BP-200, 3}, {OF-100, 0}]) is called with the 409 response"},{"given":"The CartStore after AC-39.1","id":"AC-39.2","level":"unit","then":"Every returned line has a quantity value from 1 to 99 and CartStore.count() returns 5","when":"CartStore.lines() is called"}],"ears":"When the orders API rejects an order with a 409 stock conflict, the cart shall lower each affected line to the stock now available with the message \"Only n available\", remove each affected line whose available stock is 0 with the message \"<part name> is now out of stock\", and keep all other lines.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","ASM-3","ASM-25","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CheckoutForm with a 20-character address and delivery option Standard","id":"AC-40.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is false","when":"CheckoutForm.startSubmit() is called and then CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called"},{"given":"The CheckoutForm from AC-40.1 after startSubmit()","id":"AC-40.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned value is true","when":"CheckoutForm.finishSubmit() is called and then CheckoutForm.canPlaceOrder() is called"},{"given":"A buyer at checkout with a valid cart, address and delivery option, and the orders API delaying its response by 3 seconds","id":"AC-40.3","level":"manual","then":"The button is shown disabled until the response arrives and exactly one POST /api/orders request is sent","when":"they press \"Place order\" twice within 1 second"}],"ears":"While a place-order request is in progress, the checkout shall disable \"Place order\".","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore holding 3 of BP-200 saved at unit price 12.50, and a parts API client stub returning BP-200 with price 14.00 and stock 10","id":"AC-41.1","level":"unit","then":"One call is sent to the parts client for BP-200, the returned line has unitPrice 14.00 and lineTotal 42.00, and the returned subtotal value is 42.00","when":"CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called and then CartStore.lines() and CartStore.subtotal() are called"},{"given":"A buyer whose stored cart holds BP-200 saved at £12.50, while the parts database price for BP-200 is now £14.00","id":"AC-41.2","level":"manual","then":"The unit price shown is £14.00, the subtotal shown is based on £14.00, and £12.50 is not displayed anywhere on the page","when":"they open /cart"}],"ears":"When the buyer opens the cart, the cart shall fetch the current price of each line's part from the parts API and use only those current prices for unit prices, line totals and totals.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore holding 2 of OF-100 \"Oil Filter\" and 1 of BP-200, and a parts API client stub returning OF-100 with stock 0 and BP-200 with stock 10","id":"AC-42.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned lines list contains only BP-200 with quantity value 1, the returned messages include \"Oil Filter is now out of stock\", and CartStore.count() returns 1","when":"CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called"},{"given":"A CartStore whose only line is 1 of OF-100 \"Oil Filter\", and a parts API client stub returning OF-100 with stock 0","id":"AC-42.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned lines list is empty, so no line with quantity value 0 remains","when":"CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called and then CartStore.lines() is called"}],"ears":"If the current part data fetched when the cart opens shows a cart line's part has 0 stock, then the cart shall remove that line and give the message \"<part name> is now out of stock\".","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A CartStore holding 3 of BP-200 \"Brake Pad\" saved at unit price 12.50, and a parts API client stub that fails with a network error (no response)","id":"AC-43.1","level":"unit","then":"The value returned by refresh has an error field set; the returned lines list has one BP-200 line with name \"Brake Pad\", quantity value 3, unitPrice null and lineTotal null; subtotal() returns null and totals() returns null, so the saved value 12.50 is never returned","when":"CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called and then CartStore.lines(), CartStore.subtotal() and CartStore.totals(\"STANDARD\") are called"},{"given":"A CartStore holding 3 of BP-200 saved at unit price 12.50, and a parts API client stub that returns status 500","id":"AC-43.2","level":"unit","then":"The value returned by refresh has an error field set, the returned BP-200 line has quantity value 3, unitPrice null and lineTotal null, and subtotal() returns null","when":"CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called and then CartStore.lines() and CartStore.subtotal() are called"},{"given":"The CartStore after AC-43.2, and the parts API client stub now returning BP-200 with price 14.00 and stock 10","id":"AC-43.3","level":"unit","then":"The value returned by refresh has no error field set, the returned line has unitPrice 14.00 and lineTotal 42.00, and the returned subtotal value is 42.00","when":"CartStore.refresh(partsClient) is called again and then CartStore.lines() and CartStore.subtotal() are called"},{"given":"A buyer whose stored cart holds 3 of BP-200 \"Brake Pad\" saved at £12.50, and GET /api/parts returning status 500","id":"AC-43.4","level":"manual","then":"The line is shown with name \"Brake Pad\", part number BP-200 and quantity 3; no unit price, line total, subtotal, delivery charge or total is displayed and £12.50 is not displayed anywhere on the page; an error message and a \"Try again\" button are shown; no address field, delivery option or \"Place order\" button is displayed","when":"they open /cart"},{"given":"The /cart screen from AC-43.4, and GET /api/parts now returning BP-200 with price £14.00 and stock 10","id":"AC-43.5","level":"manual","then":"The error message and \"Try again\" button are no longer shown, the unit price shown is £14.00 with line total £42.00, and the address field, delivery options and \"Place order\" button are displayed","when":"the buyer presses \"Try again\""}],"ears":"If the request to the parts API for current prices fails with a network or server error when the cart opens, then the cart shall show the cart lines without unit prices, line totals or totals, show an error message with a \"Try again\" button, and hide checkout until current prices load.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","Q-5","Q-3"]}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]},"settled":[{"decision":"If a part in the cart now has 0 stock, what should happen to that cart line? (One rule says the quantity can never go below 1. Another says it can never go above stock.) → Remove the line and show \"<part name> is now out of stock\"","how":"assumed","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-13 forces any quantity up to a minimum of 1, but REQ-14 caps it at the part's stock, so a cart line whose part now has 0 stock has two contradictory required outcomes (1 vs 0).","ref":"Q-1"},{"decision":"If the buyer retries after a network error but the first order was actually saved, how should we stop the order being placed twice? → Disable \"Place order\" while a request is in progress, and on a network error tell the buyer to check My orders before retrying","how":"assumed","kind":"critic","problem":"Retrying after a network error (REQ-24) has no duplicate-submission or idempotency protection, so an order the server already saved can be placed twice.","ref":"Q-2"},{"decision":"The cart keeps a saved copy of each price, but orders are charged at the current price. How should the cart handle a price that has changed? → Fetch the current prices from the parts API when the cart opens, and show only those","how":"assumed","kind":"critic","problem":"The cart keeps a copy of the unit price in local storage while REQ-20 charges the current server price, and no requirement covers telling the buyer when the price has changed, so the total shown can differ from the total saved.","ref":"Q-3"},{"decision":"Should the spec keep a separate requirement that the API rejects requests with no valid company-login session (status 401)? The request doesn't mention this. → Leave it out and rely on the existing company login as-is","how":"assumed","kind":"invented","problem":"The API shall reject requests with status 401 when there is no valid session token or cookie.","ref":"Q-4"},{"decision":"When the cart opens and the request to the parts API for current prices fails (network or server error), what should the cart show and allow? The saved prices must never be shown. → Show the cart lines without prices or totals, show an error message with a \"Try again\" button, and hide checkout until current prices load","how":"assumed","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-41 and REQ-42 say nothing about what the cart shows or does when the parts API call fails on cart open, even though REQ-41 says only current prices may be shown and the saved prices must never be shown (ASM-26).","ref":"Q-5"},{"decision":"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk","how":"open-risk","kind":"critic","problem":"ASM-26 and AC-41.1 need GET /api/parts filtered to the cart's part numbers in a single call, but REQ-2/4/5 and ASM-19 only define q (at least 2 characters, substring match), category, brand and page, so no defined parameter can fetch exactly the cart's parts."},{"decision":"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk","how":"open-risk","kind":"critic","problem":"When the cart opens, only lines whose part now has 0 stock are handled; a line whose stock has dropped but is still above 0 (cart quantity 5, stock now 2) is left unclamped until the 409 at Place order, and REQ-14's clamp only runs when the buyer edits the quantity."},{"decision":"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk","how":"open-risk","kind":"critic","problem":"The order is charged at the server's current price, but the price can change between cart refresh and Place order; nothing says the buyer is told or asked to confirm, so the saved total can differ from the total on screen (payments risk)."}]}